{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1CPNPmuxH9bGmUabxV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SoZy9hTiduBwa51yrZ1Dkz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-GrSuw6; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n''','''    # Intervals.icu may return neither expires_in nor refresh_token: such a token\n    # does not expire on a timer, so do not invent an expiry (None = no expiry).\n    expires_in = int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n''')\ns=s.replace('\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in,','\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in if expires_in else None,')\ns=s.replace('(expires in {expires_in}s)\")','(expires in {expires_in or \"never\"}s)\")')\ns=s.replace('if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:','if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] is None or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:')\ns=s.replace('expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))','expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None)')\n# wellness: mark expired only when Intervals rejects the token\ns=s.replace('''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})''','''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            if e.code == 401:\n                with LOCK:\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})''')\n# auth init returns JSON\ns=s.replace('''        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))''','''        # Return the URL instead of redirecting: the SPA calls this with fetch() (which\n        # carries the Bearer header) and then navigates; a plain link cannot send it.\n        self.send_json(200, {\"url\": AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")})''')\nopen('server.py','w').write(s)\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('SCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"','''# Intervals rejects the authorize request (400 invalid_request) when the CALENDAR:* scopes\n# are included; this is the set that worked on 2026-09-19. Override via env if the\n# OAuth client gets calendar access approved.\nSCOPES = os.environ.get(\"INTERVALS_SCOPES\", \"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\")''')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\na=open('static/app.js').read()\na=a.replace('<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>','<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>')\na=a.replace('''    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''','''    const cb = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (cb) cb.onclick = async () => {\n      try { location.href = (await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/init\")).url; }\n      catch (e) { root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`; }\n    };\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''')\nopen('static/app.js','w').write(a)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why Intervals.icu connection fails\n\n1. **Connect button always 401s.** It was a plain `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">`. A browser navigation cannot send the `Authorization: Bearer` header (the SPA only adds it in `fetch`), so `require_user` returned `{\"error\":\"unauthorized\"}` for everyone. Fix: `/auth/init` now returns `{url}` as JSON; the button calls it via `fetch` (with the header) and then sets `location.href`.\n2. **Authorize step 400s even with a hand-built link.** The 2026-10-02 calendar sync added `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` to `SCOPES`. Intervals answers `invalid_request` before the consent screen; the last working request (Rivera, 2026-09-19) was granted only `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ`. Fix: scopes reverted to the known-working set, overridable via `INTERVALS_SCOPES`. Caveat: I cannot reach Intervals from here, so this is inferred from the logs (the error body does not name the parameter) and untested; calendar scopes presumably need to be enabled on the OAuth client before they are re-added.\n3. **\"Reconnect\" after an hour.** Intervals' token response had no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token`. `store_connection` invented a 3600s default expiry, and the refresher then marked the connection expired with nothing to refresh. Fix: no `expires_in` now means no timer-based expiry; a connection is marked expired only if Intervals actually rejects the token (401 on wellness). The refresh path also no longer crashes on a missing `expires_in`.\n\nNot tested end to end against Intervals (no external access).\nE\npython3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('server.py').read())\"; git diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6170,"cache_read_input_tokens":22359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6170},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5909f5de-c121-405b-9fe3-12f74a24d3d9","uuid":"f751f239-19df-493c-be7e-1fe3e06cac19","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:07:38.397Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1CP2pMvYpXeL91AQtp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SoZy9hTiduBwa51yrZ1Dkz":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-GrSuw6; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\ns=open('serv