e server rejected every click. `/api/intervals/auth/init` now returns the authorize URL as JSON. The button in `static/app.js` fetches it with the header, then navigates to that URL.\n2. **Intervals returns 400 at the authorize step.** The calendar sync added `CALENDAR:READ` and `CALENDAR:WRITE` to the scopes on 2026-10-02. The last connection that worked, Rivera's on 2026-09-19, was granted only `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ`. I reverted `config.py` to that set, and `INTERVALS_SCOPES` can override it. This one is inferred from the logs, because the 400 body doesn't say which parameter it rejects. If it's wrong, the calendar scopes may need approving on the OAuth client first.\n3. **\"Reconnect\" after an hour.** Intervals returned neither `expires_in` nor a refresh token. The code assumed a 3600-second lifetime and then marked the connection expired with nothing to refresh. A token with no stated lifetime is now treated as not expiring. A connection is marked expired only when Intervals actually returns 401. The refresh path also no longer crashes when `expires_in` is missing.\n\nCalendar sync won't be able to get calendar access until those scopes are approved and re-added.","ttft_ms":1630,"type":"result","duration_ms":30621,"uuid":"3204048c-2e14-4e98-9877-26ef9bfbe429","ttft_stream_ms":1363,"time_to_request_ms":33,"first_content_frame_ms":1363,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":3803,"cacheReadInputTokens":88303,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14662,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.10552429999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":969,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
